Show that every angle inscribed in a semicircle is a right angle, as suggested by Figure 1.46.

To prove this remark, we'll make use of Figure 1.47, where a and b are "radius vectors" with tails at the center of the circle. 
We need only show that a-b (a vector along one ray of the angle in question) is perpendicular to -a-b (a vector along the orther ray). 
In other words, we wish to show that 

		(a-b)*(-a-b) = 0

we have 

		(a-b)*(-a-b) = (-1)(a-b)*(a+b), 

by property 4 of dot products, 

			=(-1)((a-b)*a+(a-b)*b)
			=(-4)(a*a-b*a+a*b-b*b)
			=(-1)(||a||²-||b||²),

by properties 2 and 4, 

			= 0,

since both a and b are radius vectors (and therefore have the same length, namely, the radius of the circle)

